From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015-d21: Run the touch clock at 32768 Hz

The D21 ADT asks for function-clock_enable = KLCT(0x08, 0x64, 0x8000),
a 32768 Hz touch reference, and the C1F5E firmware programs the
controller FLL for it (0x10003060 = 6099, 0x10003518 = 1). The t8015
dtsi carries the iPhone X rate of 24 MHz, so on D21 the divider was 1
and the controller got 24 MHz (live: PMGR 0x78000 = 0x00080001).
The iPhone 7 boards already override this to 32768.

With this, five fresh boots and ten module reloads on the iPhone 8 Plus
all delivered touch.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d21.dts |  9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d21.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d21.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d21.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d21.dts
@@ -60,3 +60,12 @@
 		touchscreen-size-y = <1920>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The D21 ADT's function-clock_enable asks for a 32768 Hz touch reference
+ * (KLCT 0x08, 0x64, 0x8000); the controller firmware's FLL setup assumes
+ * it. The t8015 default is the iPhone X's 24 MHz.
+ */
+&touchclk {
+	clock-frequency = <32768>;
+};
